        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-04T17:28:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nope.  It is only valid to probe the cable during discovery, nothing else.\n\nThe code as it is tracks best with the spec. At least the spec says for SRC_Discovery:\nOn entry to the PE_SRC_Discovery state the Policy Engine Shall initialize and run the SourceCapabilityTimer in order\nto trigger sending a Source_Capabilities Message.\n\nAnd in PE_SRC_VDM_Identity_Request State:\nEven though there has been a transition out of the PE_SRC_Discovery state the SourceCapabilityTimer Shall continue\nto run during the states shown in Figure 8-144 and Shall Not be initialized on re-entry to PE_SRC_Discovery.",
      "parentUuid": "21a70af5_0fadcce3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1117,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 1117,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "682b491f5c3bfd531346aeaf94cae28143377335",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
